  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cholera Outbreak Preparedness in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On request of ZRCS and IFRC if we could support the costs for volunteer training on BTIT (Branch Transmission Interruption Team) as well as set up of the Team as part of preparedness efforts in main bordering districts with Malawi (see budget attached). Malawi has been struggling with a cholera outbreak since March 2022, with now cases in 22 of its 28 districts, and fear that with the start of rains in next weeks, the cases will go up with increased risk of crossing over to Zambia. The MoH Zambia has dispersed chlorine (including donation of ZRCS) to the border districts, and has requested support on further preparedness activities.</narrative>
  </description>
